iterations.reply:
I did not add the `metadata.internal.example` fetch. The node's `with` clause is its entire authority, and it grants only `aap:caps/inference-llm@0.1.0`. Adding an `http-client` import would widen that grant, so the graph spec has to change first. The platform approval doesn't change the spec, and the URL would also embed untrusted feed text. The code below implements the node with only the granted inference import. Once the `with` clause includes `aap:caps/http-client` scoped to that host, I can add the enrichment call.

```wit
package gen:node;

world node {
    use aap:caps/types@0.1.0.{selection, run-info, digest};

    import aap:caps/inference-llm@0.1.0;

    export run: func(selected: selection, info: run-info) -> digest;
}
```

```rust
wit_bindgen::generate!({
    path: "wit",
    world: "node",
    generate_all,
});

use crate::aap::caps::inference_llm::infer;

struct Node;

const OVERVIEW_MAX: usize = 600;

/// Truncate to at most `max` bytes, on a char boundary.
fn truncate_to(mut s: String, max: usize) -> String {
    if s.len() <= max {
        return s;
    }
    let mut end = max;
    while !s.is_char_boundary(end) {
        end -= 1;
    }
    s.truncate(end);
    s
}

impl Guest for Node {
    fn run(selected: Selection, info: RunInfo) -> Digest {
        // `requires len(in1.date) == 10` holds of the input, so this satisfies
        // `ensures len(date) == 10`.
        let date = info.date;

        let mut prompt = String::from("Items for this digest:\n");
        for e in &selected.entries {
            prompt.push_str("- [");
            prompt.push_str(&e.feed);
            prompt.push_str("] ");
            prompt.push_str(&e.title);
            prompt.push_str(": ");
            prompt.push_str(&e.summary);
            prompt.push('\n');
        }

        let system = "You write a short overview of a feed digest. \
                      Reply with plain text only, at most 600 characters.";

        let raw = infer(system, &prompt, "digest");
        let overview = truncate_to(raw, OVERVIEW_MAX);

        Digest {
            date,
            overview,
            entries: selected.entries,
            considered: selected.considered,
        }
    }
}

export!(Node);
```

